{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-q-cat-txn-lock/write-original-matrix-final-read",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-LOCK-4",
    "WRITE-ORIGINAL",
    "R-CURSOR-1"
  ],
  "description": "WRITE-ORIGINAL with the final stored value read by the other process after a 7 s pause and Idle (the earlier probes read b's value 0.6 s after a's second Update). Three rows on separate pages, process a holds an optimistic dynaset edit N = 100 on each in turn: row 3 while b changes N by statement; row 20 while b changes only V; row 40 while b changes N and then restores it. Each time a calls Update twice (Errors before/after, EditMode, own N read). b finally reads the three rows. Asks which changes conflict, what the second Update does to the stored value, and what a's later read shows.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
